      "schema_version": "aspr_gear",
      "text": "This study examines how APOA1 binding protein (AIBP) promotes lymphatic endothelial cell fate and lymphangiogenesis by reducing plasma-membrane cholesterol, disrupting caveolae-mediated CAV-1 inhibition, and enhancing VEGFR3 signalling. The final paper combines zebrafish, mESC-derived lymphatic endothelial cell, human lymphatic endothelial cell, and mouse models, including VEGFR3 and CAV-1 perturbations and a mouse lymphedema-recovery experiment. Earlier concerns about morphology, assay interpretation, nomenclature, atorvastatin rescue, human-sample panels, and abstract wording were addressed in the final state and are retained only as audit history."
    },
